    lever value in `cfg` is a recognized member before running. A lever whose value doesn't match any
    dispatch branch silently falls through to a default/no-op - the experiment runs, writes a
    scoreboard row, and looks like a real test of that lever when it changed nothing. This has actually
    happened (an unwired lever burned a full evaluation before being caught by a manual review, not by
    the runner) - fail loudly here instead of relying on someone noticing.
    """
    raise NotImplementedError("Implement validate_method() - hard-fail on any cfg lever value the "
